# Project Structure & Routing Rules

## Monorepo Architecture
This is a Turborepo monorepo with:
- `apps/core/` - Back office portal (React + Vite)
- `apps/dealer/` - Dealer portal (React + Vite) 
- `apps/server/` - Backend API (NestJS + Prisma + PostgreSQL)
- `packages/` - Shared packages (UI components, hooks, utilities, configs)

## URL-to-Folder Mapping (File-based Routing)
Follow these exact patterns:
- `/user` → `user/page.tsx`
- `/user/:user_id` → `user/[user_id]/page.tsx` 
- `/user/:user_id/profile` → `user/[user_id]/profile/page.tsx`

## Feature Folder Blueprint
Every feature follows this structure:
```
feature/
  _hooks/         ← remote data & mutations
  _contents/      ← presentational components only
  schemas.ts      ← Zod schema + exported TS types
  page.tsx        ← route entry point
```

## Underscore Prefix Rule
- **Use `_` prefix**: Only for directories that are NOT pages/routes (`_hooks/`, `_contents/`)
- **No `_` prefix**: For route directories (`feature/`, `[param]/`, `nested-route/`)

## Required Files
- Every route MUST have a `page.tsx` file as entry point
- Every folder MUST have an `index.ts` barrel file for exports
- Every feature MUST have a `schemas.ts` file for type definitions

